null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110043","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110043","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110043.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110043.patch","merged_at":"2025-09-02T00:12:11Z"},"body":"Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110042 - a regression introduced in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99680 caused external debuggers using the legacy `scene:inspect_object` command to break. This breaks external debuggers like the vscode godot plugin.\r\n\r\nDetails:\r\n\r\nThe `scene:inspect_object` command was replaced with `scene:inspect_objects` (plural) which changed the API from accepting a single object ID to requiring an array of IDs plus a boolean parameter. This broke external debuggers that relied on the original single-object API. Added backward-compatible proxy handlers on both engine and editor sides that convert the legacy single-object format to the new multi-object format internally, ensuring external debuggers continue to work without modification while preserving all new functionality.\r\n\r\nChanges:\r\nEngine: Added inspect_object handler that processes single ID and returns single object response\r\nEditor: Added scene:inspect_object response handler that converts single object to array format\r\nDebug Adapter: Added support for legacy single-object response format","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/u